OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CNostalgic wartime music
OL,4,Caccompanies Pages from Ceefax on VE Day
OL,5,Canniversary
OL,6,
OL,7,FARCHIVE: YouTube: tony d
OL,8,
OL,9,FThe fortieth anniversary of VE Day in
OL,10,F1985 brought a little surprise for Pres
OL,11,Ffans.
OL,12,
OL,13,FThe regular test card and Ceefax music
OL,14,Fon BBC Television was replaced for the
OL,15,Fday.
OL,16,
OL,17,FInstead nostalgic wartime music was
OL,18,Fplayed featuring big bands and artistes
OL,19,Ffrom the 40s such as Glenn Miller, The
OL,20,FSquadronaires and Vera Lynn.
OL,21,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,125,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12402
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F124A1768699310
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}          G2/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CNostalgic wartime music
OL,4,Caccompanies Pages from Ceefax on VE Day
OL,5,Canniversary
OL,6,
OL,7,FThe special music got its first outing
OL,8,Fon BBC One accompanying Ceefax AM
OL,9,Fbefore Breakfast Time. Inevitably
OL,10,Fthough, VE Day coverage and sport meant
OL,11,Fthere were no daytime gaps on BBC One
OL,12,Fthat day.
OL,13,
OL,14,FHowever there was plenty of time for
OL,15,Fthe music on BBC Two.
OL,16,
OL,17,FFirst it appeared with the test card at
OL,18,F8.52am before accompanying Ceefax
OL,19,Fthrough all the main daytime gaps up
OL,20,Funtil 5.30pm.
OL,21,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,125,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12403
SC,0003
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F124A1768699310
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}          G3/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CNostalgic wartime music
OL,4,Caccompanies Pages from Ceefax on VE Day
OL,5,Canniversary
OL,6,
OL,7,FThe wartime music was also heard during
OL,8,Fsome of the longer intervalsB between
OL,9,Fschools programmes during the Daytime
OL,10,Fon Two sequence.
OL,11,
OL,12,FIt was a lovely, thoughtful touch by
OL,13,FPresentation.
OL,14,
OL,15,FThe music was, of course, not
OL,16,Fpublicised in advance but I wonder if
OL,17,Fsome from the wartime generation came
OL,18,Facross it by chance and appreciated the
OL,19,Feffort.
OL,20,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,125,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12404
SC,0004
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F124A1768699310
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}          G4/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CNostalgic wartime music
OL,4,Caccompanies Pages from Ceefax on VE Day
OL,5,Canniversary
OL,6,
OL,7,FIt is worth reflecting on the fact that
OL,8,Flistening to wartime music in 1985 is
OL,9,Fthe equivalent of playing a Duran Duran
OL,10,Falbum today.
OL,11,
OL,12,FAs far as we know, this is the only
OL,13,Ftime regular test card or Ceefax music
OL,14,Fwas replaced in this way.
OL,15,
OL,16,FChristmas music was played through much
OL,17,Fof December and mindful staff often
OL,18,Fmade sure the classical music tapes
OL,19,Fwere played on sombre or noteworthy
OL,20,Foccasions.
OL,21,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,125,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12405
SC,0005
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F124A1768699310
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}          G5/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CNostalgic wartime music
OL,4,Caccompanies Pages from Ceefax on VE Day
OL,5,Canniversary
OL,6,
OL,7,FTwo special tapes of sombre light
OL,8,Finstrumental music were compiled
OL,9,Fspecifically to accompany Ceefax during
OL,10,Fthe Falklands War although they
OL,11,Fremained in normal use for more than
OL,12,Ftwo years afterwards.
OL,13,
OL,14,FHowever the VE Day music was different.
OL,15,FIt was an attempt to add to the mood of
OL,16,Fan important day.
OL,17,
OL,18,FThe 40th anniversary of VE Day was the
OL,19,Ffirst to be marked quite so
OL,20,Fextensively.
OL,21,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,125,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12406
SC,0006
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F124A1768699310
OL,1,W{$~sj5j5h7}j7}          G6/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CNostalgic wartime music
OL,4,Caccompanies Pages from Ceefax on VE Day
OL,5,Canniversary
OL,6,
OL,7,FIn those days Presentation was often
OL,8,Fmindful of trying to set the right
OL,9,Ftone. It was about far more than
OL,10,Fmarketing and playout.
OL,11,
OL,12,FIn its own way, this helped to define
OL,13,Fthe character of BBC Television and
OL,14,Fgive it a distinctive feel.
OL,15,
OL,16,FAfter I write this article, a beautiful
OL,17,Ffootnote emerged.
OL,18,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,125,120,200,300,0,100
PN,12407
SC,0007
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F124A1768699310
