OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!/*%/*-'Q(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GFEATURES CNostalgic wartime music
OL,4,Caccompanies Pages from Ceefax on VE Day
OL,5,Canniversary
OL,6,
OL,7,FThe special VE Day music was played
OL,8,Fagain on the 50th anniversary of VE Day
OL,9,Fin 1995.
OL,10,
OL,11,FBy then Ceefax was confined to short
OL,12,Fslots, usually of 15 minutes, before
OL,13,Fthe first programme of the day.
OL,14,
OL,15,FThe opening on 8th May is particularly
OL,16,Feffective.B
OL,17,
OL,18,FThe music carried on briefly over the
OL,19,Fclock as Roger Maude announced a
OL,20,Fspecial edition of Breakfast News.B
OL,21,
OL,23,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BRewind CNat Radio FNat Sport
FL,125,120,200,300,0,100
